			"widgets_values":[
				"A vertical, cinematic masterpiece capturing the serene melancholy of the Qingming Festival (Pure Brightness), rendered in a hyper-detailed, ethereal style reminiscent of classical Chinese ink wash paintings fused with modern digital realism. The scene is dominated by a misty, jade-green palette — cool teals, muted emeralds, and soft grays — evoking the damp, quiet atmosphere of spring rain. Towering, jagged mountains rise majestically on either side, their peaks shrouded in swirling fog that diffuses the ambient light into a soft, luminous glow. Delicate, almost translucent rain streaks fall vertically across the entire frame, catching the light like fine silver threads, enhancing the sense of gentle motion and stillness.\n\nIn the foreground, a calm, mirror-like river reflects the surrounding landscape with perfect clarity — the silhouettes of pine trees, the distant hills, and even the falling rain are mirrored beneath the surface. Atop a dark, muscular water buffalo standing waist-deep in the water sits a small child, barefoot and dressed in simple, earth-toned traditional garments — perhaps a pale pink or ochre tunic and loose trousers — their posture relaxed, gazing ahead as if lost in contemplation. The child’s skin appears smooth and dew-kissed, subtly highlighted by the diffused daylight filtering through the clouds above.\n\nThe background is layered with dense forests of tall, slender conifers and broadleaf trees, their leaves glistening with moisture, creating rich textural contrast against the softer mists. A single red circular seal stamp bearing white Chinese characters (“二十四节气” — Twenty-Four Solar Terms) floats near the center-right, adding a touch of cultural authenticity and visual warmth to the cool-toned composition. Dominating the upper third of the image are two large, bold calligraphic characters — “清明” (Qingming) — painted in flowing white brushstrokes with subtle ink bleed effects, giving them an organic, hand-painted feel. Below, smaller text reads “[清明·时节]” and “清明时节情谊浓，踏青祭祖念先人,” followed by the English translation “PURE BRIGHTNESS” in clean, minimalist sans-serif font.\n\nThe lighting is soft and directional, coming from behind the mountain peaks, casting long, gentle shadows across the valley floor while illuminating the mist with a heavenly radiance. The overall mood is one of peaceful reverence, quiet nostalgia, and natural harmony — a moment suspended between memory and presence, where nature and tradition intertwine under the whispering rain. Every element — from the texture of the buffalo’s wet hide to the ripples distorting the reflection — is rendered with meticulous attention to detail, inviting the viewer into a world both dreamlike and deeply real."
			],
